"""Pillar guide (project guide 1 of the evening-routine queue): harden Active Directory Certificate Services (AD CS) as a Tier 0 system.
Covers why AD CS is Tier 0, inventory and assessment (Locksmith, Certipy, Defender for Identity), template fixes (ESC1-4, ESC9, ESC13, ESC15),
CA settings and permissions (ESC6, ESC7, ESC11, ESC16), NTLM relay to enrollment endpoints (ESC8, KB5005413), strong certificate mapping
(KB5014754, Schannel, ESC10, ESC14), Tier 0 operation and backup, auditing and detection, troubleshooting, incident response and rollback.
Fact-checked on 2026-10-31 against Microsoft Support (KB5014754, KB5005413), Microsoft Learn (Defender for Identity, certutil, ADCSAdministration,
ADCSDeployment, audit policy), the Microsoft Security Blog post of 2026-10-30 on ESC1/ESC8 intrusions, and the SpecterOps / Certipy research.
ESC numbers follow the community taxonomy (SpecterOps "Certified Pre-Owned" and the Certipy wiki); Microsoft uses the same labels in Secure Score.
Text in `backticks` renders as <code>. 'rec' = recipe ids, 'tools' = /tools/ ids, 'sec' = cyber ids, 'guides' = other guide slugs.
Attack tools are named for authorised assessment of your own environment only."""

