INTRO = [
    "Active Directory Certificate Services is the quiet back door of most Windows estates. An enterprise CA that is trusted in the NTAuth store can issue certificates "
    "that domain controllers accept for Kerberos logon (PKINIT). One misconfigured template, one CA flag or one NTLM-enabled enrollment web page is enough for a "
    "normal user to obtain a certificate for a Domain Admin or a domain controller, and that certificate keeps working after the password is reset.",
    "This is not theory. On 30 October 2026 Microsoft Threat Intelligence described two intrusions that started with help-desk impersonation in Teams and Quick Assist "
    "and then went straight for AD CS: one abused an ESC1 template to get certificates for privileged accounts and run DCSync, the other used PetitPotam coercion "
    "and NTLM relay to Web Enrollment (ESC8) to get a domain controller certificate.",
    "This guide treats the PKI as what it is, a Tier 0 system, and walks the full programme: inventory and assessment, template and CA fixes, relay protection, "
    "strong certificate mapping on domain controllers, Tier 0 operation and backup, auditing and detection, and finally troubleshooting, incident response and rollback.",
]
